From 242b0de0292a244919e23aa1749572193412cf1f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jurulz <60669313+jurulz@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 14:20:24 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 4/6] F-Zero AX: Publish cabinet outputs and add built-in force
 feedback

NetworkOutputs: serve the MAME/Flycast style network outputs protocol on 127.0.0.1:8000 (UDP announce on 8001) with the lamps (LampStart, LampView1-4, LampBoost/LampLeader), mamerun, WheelServo, WheelInit and every wheel command (WheelCmd<N>, WheelCnt<N>), so cabinet software such as BackForceFeeder can use them. WheelForceFeedback: a thread that computes a force from the target position requested by the game and the real wheel position (Control Stick X of pad 1) and sends it to the Constant output of a force-feedback device through the controller interface. Settings are reloaded from User/Config/FZeroFFB.ini; orders and state go through FZeroFFB_cmd.txt and FZeroFFB_status.txt. Disabled unless enabled = 1.
---
